(Bug #69's replacement half. The tag the result carries when the
 substitution fires is the replacement's own, so a `value` replacement hands
 over its runtime tag exactly as a literal hands over its static one.)

a value called swap is "X".
print each item from [1, "-"] treating "-" as swap.

(A value on both sides of the clause.)
a value called probe is "-".
print each item from [1, "-"] treating probe as swap.

(The replacement's tag really is the one that comes out: a value holding a
 number, substituted into a mixed list, prints as the number it is.)
a value called nine is 9.
print each item from [1, "-"] treating "-" as nine.
